{
  "$comment": [
    "FBL-020-R6 §1.4 — THE ALLOWLIST OF PARTIAL MIGRATION CHAINS.",
    "",
    "scripts/migrate.ts applies migrations/ . Pointing it at any other directory is how a",
    "partial or altered chain could reach a database, so that is an OPT-IN mode: the caller",
    "must name a chain declared here, and every file in the directory it hands over must be",
    "declared here BY NAME and match one of the canonical-LF sha256 digests declared under",
    "that name. An unnamed chain, an unknown name, an extra file, a missing required file or",
    "a body whose digest is not on the list all REFUSE.",
    "",
    "R6 §1.4 WITHDREW TWO ADMISSION RULES AND THIS FILE NO LONGER CARRIES EITHER.",
    "  * `reserved-probe-filenames` admitted any body under a declared filename. The bodies",
    "    tests/migration-ledger.test.ts actually writes are four one-line statements, so all",
    "    four are declared below by digest, under the filename each may occupy.",
    "  * `single-statement-deletion` admitted any body reachable from canonical 057 by",
    "    deleting one contiguous span holding one `;`. The twelve deletions",
    "    scripts/upgrade-negative-controls.ts performs are deterministic, so all twelve are",
    "    declared below by the digest of the RESULTING body — and a thirteenth is refused.",
    "scripts/migration-fixture-chains.ts REFUSES this file if any chain carries the withdrawn",
    "keys (kind, filename_pattern, filenames, mutated_file, mutated_file_canonical_sha256) or",
    "declares a filename with no digest, because a filename with no digest IS filename-only",
    "admission.",
    "",
    "NOTHING HERE WEAKENS A CHECK. Every refusal in the runner — a NULL or unsupported",
    "checksum, a missing migration body, a body that no longer matches its recorded digest —",
    "applies identically in fixture mode. What a chain grants is only the right to use a",
    "restricted directory; bodies of already-applied migrations that the restricted directory",
    "does not carry are still resolved from migrations/ and still verified there.",
    "",
    "Digests are sha256 over the CANONICAL-LF text, the same value the ledger records. A",
    "digest of the working bytes would differ between a Windows checkout (CRLF) and CI (LF)",
    "and could not be pinned at all.",
    "",
    "`required: false` means the fixture may or may not carry the file at a given moment — the",
    "ledger battery writes and removes a third probe migration as it drives the refusals. It",
    "does NOT relax the checksum: an optional file that is present must still match a declared",
    "digest."
  ],
